# Type Safety and Shared Types Guidelines

## Core Principles

- **Single Source of Truth**: All shared types, enums, and interfaces must live in `@org/commons`
- **Zero Magic Strings**: Always use enums for predefined string values
- **Strict Type Enforcement**: No `any` types or type assertions unless absolutely necessary
- **Cross-Module Consistency**: Frontend and backend must use the same type definitions

## Type Organization in Commons

```typescript
// ✅ DO: Keep related types together in a single file
// @org/commons/lib/booth.types.ts
export enum BoothEventType {
  SESSION_START = 'session_start',
  PRINTING = 'printing',
}

export interface BoothLog {
  id: string;
  boothEventType: BoothEventType;
}

// ❌ DON'T: Duplicate type definitions across modules
// frontend/src/types/booth.ts - WRONG!
export interface BoothLog {
  id: string;
  type: string; // Should use BoothEventType from commons
}
```

